# applications/lumenetes/Dockerfile is the only build that uses the repo
# root as its context (needed to see the root module's pkg/ source,
# resolved locally via the repo-root go.work workspace rather than a
# go.mod "replace" directive) - every other app's image is scoped to its
# own applications/<name>/ subdirectory and never sees this file.
#
# Allow-list, not deny-list: this Dockerfile's `go build` only ever needs
# the root module's go.mod/go.sum, go.work/go.work.sum (workspace-mode
# resolution - go build finds go.work by walking up from the current
# directory, same as go.mod, so it must be present in the build context
# too), pkg/ (the actual root-module source it imports), and
# applications/lumenetes/ itself. Everything else in this monorepo -
# other apps, os/, cli/, docs, etc. - is irrelevant to this build but was
# previously NOT excluded (the old version of this file was a short
# deny-list covering only a few known-large dirs), so literally any change
# anywhere in the repo busted this image's build-cache and triggered a
# full rebuild+push on every `homelab up`. Denying everything by default
# and re-allowing only what's actually needed fixes that at the root.
*
!go.mod
!go.sum
!go.work
!go.work.sum
!pkg/
!applications/lumenetes/
